  "_title": "Subtraction is the same circuit",
  "_description": "One extra 74HC86 turns the adder into an adder-subtractor. The mode switch feeds the XOR bank AND the carry-in at once: with it open you get A + B, with it closed every B bit flips and a 1 enters the bottom, which is two’s complement — so the machine subtracts without a single new adder. The red LED now means \"no borrow\": it lights when A is greater than or equal to B.",
  "_category": "logic",
  "_difficulty": 4,
  "_stage": "L8"
}
